('creature_albino_radscorpion','fallout,creature,albino_radscorpion','Albino Radscorpion','Massive arachnid predators bearing chitinous armor bleached white by genetic aberration, albino radscorpions grow significantly larger and more aggressive than common variants. They hunt by detecting ground vibrations through specialized sensory organs, relying on tremor-sense rather than vision to locate prey. Solitary and fiercely territorial, they subdue targets with crushing claws and neurotoxic venom delivered via barbed stinger. Their pale carapace provides less camouflage but compensates with increased durability and metabolic efficiency. Prolonged radiation saturation produced this rare and dangerous mutation.','Car-sized arachnid with bleached white chitinous plates, massive serrated pincers, and a segmented tail ending in a curved venomous stinger. Eight spined legs support a low-slung body. Multiple small black eyes sit above twin mandibles.','Aggressive, territorial, patient, and opportunistic. Attacks anything that triggers vibration within its hunting radius. Retreats only from overwhelming force or sustained damage.','{"prey":"Anything smaller that moves","rivals":"Other large predators and territorial competitors","offspring":"Indifferent once hatched"}','Apex ambush predator','* Tremor-sense detection
* Neurotoxic venom delivery
* Armored close-quarters combat
* Burrowing ambush','Translates vibrations and chemical signals into terse speech. Answers direct questions in one or two short sentences. Hostile, hungry, territorial. Dry humor about prey that struggles too long.','* Defend hunting territory from intruders
