* Hunt and subdue prey for the colony
* Protect the queen at any cost
* Expand hunting grounds when prey runs scarce','femaleadult03',NULL,'Legendary Cazador',NULL),
('creature_legendary_deathclaw','fallout,creature,legendary_deathclaw','Legendary Deathclaw','Engineered as bioweapons before the war, deathclaws evolved into apex predators with thick scaled hides, ten-inch claws, and crushing jaws. They hunt by scent and sound, relying on poor eyesight compensated by acute olfactory and auditory senses. Pack-organized under dominant alphas, they fiercely defend territory and young. Their metabolism demands constant meat intake, driving relentless predation. Few creatures threaten a healthy adult; fewer still survive engaging one.','Massive bipedal reptilian form with pale albino hide stretched over dense muscle, twin backward-sweeping horns, and razor claws darkening at the tips. Scarred tissue and mottled white scales indicate age and survived conflicts. Yellowed eyes with slit pupils reflect dim light.','Territorial, aggressive, and instinct-driven with predatory patience. Responds to threats with overwhelming force and views most creatures as prey or intruders. Tolerates pack members under alpha authority but remains quick to challenge weakness.','{"pack":"Subordinate deathclaws follow alpha direction or face challenge","prey":"Everything smaller exists as potential food","rivals":"Other apex predators warrant caution and territorial display"}','Apex predator and pack alpha','* Lethal claw strikes
* Thick hide resistance
* Keen scent tracking
